WEBVTT

00:54.220 --> 00:56.014
Look at the leaves falling down.

00:56.973 --> 00:58.308
So pretty.

01:00.477 --> 01:01.811
You look so good.

01:05.065 --> 01:07.901
- Hey, wait for me!
- Catch up already.

01:10.111 --> 01:12.363
Seoul's current temperature
is at 21 degrees.

01:12.447 --> 01:16.201
Relative humidity, 43 percent.

01:17.285 --> 01:20.872
The North Pacific air mass
has moved on from Korea,

01:21.748 --> 01:26.669
taking the heat and humidity away,
and leaving perfect autumn weather.

01:29.672 --> 01:32.592
The migratory anticyclone
comes from the west this time of year,

01:32.675 --> 01:34.302
bringing this weather.

01:34.969 --> 01:36.387
When it's like this,

01:36.471 --> 01:39.307
there are a million things
to do outside, but I…

01:52.695 --> 01:54.989
can't do any with a broken heart.

04:05.286 --> 04:06.913
I never even gave her a real present.

04:12.585 --> 04:15.463
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

04:29.519 --> 04:30.478
Hey?

04:31.062 --> 04:32.146
It's Ha-kyung.

04:33.273 --> 04:35.984
The lotion you left,
should I throw it away?

04:36.067 --> 04:39.070
Uh, no, I'd still use it.

04:40.154 --> 04:41.906
Okay. I'll save it.

04:46.953 --> 04:48.246
The chargers

04:48.329 --> 04:51.666
that are plugged in at the window,
they're all yours?

04:51.749 --> 04:54.919
Oh, no, there's one that belongs
to Mr. Um, the black one.

04:59.966 --> 05:01.926
There's more than one black one.

05:02.510 --> 05:04.721
I'll pack them all.
And you two can figure it out.

05:05.305 --> 05:06.264
Okay.

05:08.016 --> 05:12.812
Hey, if you're gathering all my stuff,
you can leave it for now.

05:13.813 --> 05:14.814
I'll come later--

05:14.897 --> 05:18.151
It's fine. It's almost done.
I'll bring everything to Headquarters.

05:18.735 --> 05:20.111
I can come, it's heavy.

05:20.778 --> 05:22.655
- I'll stop by and--
- You don't have to.

05:22.739 --> 05:23.740
That's all.

06:12.080 --> 06:17.126
EPISODE 14
MIGRATORY ANTICYCLONE

06:50.827 --> 06:53.663
Director! Director!

07:03.339 --> 07:07.135
Are you here for your stuff?
I told you I'd bring it to you. Hang on.

07:07.218 --> 07:08.970
Hey, something's wrong.

07:09.637 --> 07:10.596
What?

07:10.680 --> 07:12.849
They found out. About the two of us.

07:13.975 --> 07:14.976
Wh-what?

07:15.059 --> 07:16.686
That we were together.

07:17.812 --> 07:18.855
Huh?

07:22.984 --> 07:25.486
Well, I heard
that you're dating Director Jin.

07:26.946 --> 07:27.864
What?

07:27.947 --> 07:29.907
So, when did it start?
While we were there?

07:31.033 --> 07:33.828
Wait. No, uh… Who did you hear that from?

07:33.911 --> 07:35.496
Nobody, really.

07:35.580 --> 07:37.832
Everyone on the team knew, I was the last.

07:38.749 --> 07:40.460
Everyone, how?

07:40.543 --> 07:41.752
I don't know.

07:42.712 --> 07:44.338
That I was dating you.

07:45.047 --> 07:47.258
The whole team knows about what went on.

07:47.341 --> 07:49.302
You're seriously saying that…

07:49.385 --> 07:51.554
You're really sure everyone knows
that we dated?

07:51.637 --> 07:55.433
Yeah, I do. And by now,
the rumor's spread to all of the KMA.

07:55.516 --> 07:56.809
What?

07:57.393 --> 07:58.436
Eomma!

08:03.900 --> 08:06.527
I just knew. I knew.

08:06.611 --> 08:08.070
How long have you been here?

08:08.154 --> 08:10.990
So you two had
a little office romance, didn't you?

08:11.073 --> 08:13.826
- Eomma, no--
- Oh, I really just knew

08:13.910 --> 08:15.203
something was going on.

08:17.914 --> 08:20.291
- No way. We're not--
- Not what, huh?

08:21.209 --> 08:23.252
I also knew that you would deny it.

08:23.336 --> 08:26.005
So I brought my undeniable proof.

08:32.220 --> 08:35.431
Take a good look. Still deny it?

09:10.007 --> 09:13.427
FATHER

09:22.144 --> 09:24.021
So, what's his family do?

09:24.981 --> 09:26.107
It doesn't matter.

09:28.276 --> 09:30.236
A mother has the right
to know things like that.

09:31.195 --> 09:32.738
Mom, it's of no concern to you.

09:32.822 --> 09:33.948
Why is that?

09:35.408 --> 09:37.493
'Cause it's old news. We called it off.

09:37.577 --> 09:38.703
Why?

09:38.786 --> 09:40.413
"If Mom thinks we broke up,
she won't snoop

09:40.496 --> 09:42.790
- and she'll leave us alone"?
- Ugh, Eomma!

09:42.873 --> 09:43.916
Is he Level Eight or Nine?

09:44.000 --> 09:45.960
Ugh, come on!

09:46.043 --> 09:48.212
You have to look at it for what it is.

09:49.422 --> 09:53.050
He's already off to a bad start
since he's got to be below you.

09:53.134 --> 09:54.844
He's younger, so it's all right.

09:54.927 --> 09:57.388
We won't count that,
and hope he makes up for it.

09:58.180 --> 09:59.432
College?

09:59.515 --> 10:01.100
Parents are alive? Do you know?

10:01.183 --> 10:02.852
Where does live? And where did he grow up?

10:02.935 --> 10:04.312
I told you it's over.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.272
I have to know

10:06.355 --> 10:08.441
just what kind of family
he was raised with.

10:08.524 --> 10:10.443
So I don't say the wrong thing.

10:10.526 --> 10:12.278
How can I make a good impression on them?

10:12.361 --> 10:14.614
I don't wanna say something rude.

10:14.697 --> 10:16.741
I told you, Eomma, we broke up!

10:16.824 --> 10:18.618
You talk like I'm so great,

10:18.701 --> 10:22.455
and I went into it thinking I was, too,
but he dumped me. Do you get it?

10:22.538 --> 10:24.498
There's no way.
That's absolutely impossible.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.793
Find out his birthday, the date and time.

10:27.877 --> 10:28.711
Ugh, Eomma!

10:30.087 --> 10:32.632
What? I wanna know if you're compatible.

10:32.715 --> 10:34.675
Ugh! Stop it!

10:36.552 --> 10:38.471
Ugh, now I have a headache.

10:38.971 --> 10:43.267
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

11:11.128 --> 11:12.380
How's it going?

11:17.009 --> 11:19.136
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:21.889 --> 11:24.517
How's your mom? Did you fill her in?

11:24.600 --> 11:25.518
FATHER

11:32.733 --> 11:35.152
The person you are calling
is currently unavailable…

11:35.236 --> 11:37.905
He never answers his phone.

11:37.988 --> 11:39.240
Can you tell us what happened?

11:39.323 --> 11:42.952
I was driving in the lane closest
to the sidewalk.

11:43.035 --> 11:44.161
I wasn't going fast at all.

11:44.245 --> 11:46.747
And then, that guy just jumped out
into the road.

11:46.831 --> 11:49.500
There wasn't any way
for me to swerve or anything.

11:49.583 --> 11:52.086
- Oh, we got another fucking idiot.
- I didn't do anything wrong.

11:53.045 --> 11:55.381
You're really saying
you did nothing wrong?

11:55.464 --> 11:57.758
You hit me 'cause you were speeding.

11:57.842 --> 12:00.052
Maybe I was wrong for crossing the street.

12:00.136 --> 12:01.762
You did nothing wrong,
and I look like this?

12:02.471 --> 12:04.056
- I--
- How did you do nothing wrong!

12:07.685 --> 12:10.563
Ah, shit.

12:23.075 --> 12:24.118
Okay.

12:29.248 --> 12:31.834
Oh, I made breakfast. We can eat together.

12:32.418 --> 12:34.420
I'm not that hungry this morning.

12:34.503 --> 12:36.380
Uh, Yu-jin,
I made the dumpling soup you like.

12:36.464 --> 12:38.090
Look. It's good.

12:39.175 --> 12:41.427
Uh… Sorry.

12:41.510 --> 12:43.721
I'm not feeling great. I can't today.

12:44.513 --> 12:45.473
Ah.

12:59.987 --> 13:01.030
Yu-jin.

13:01.989 --> 13:03.073
Yeah?

13:04.450 --> 13:05.493
I wanted to let you know,

13:05.576 --> 13:09.872
we can register things later,
if you want to.

13:11.749 --> 13:13.793
Time's not a big deal.

13:13.876 --> 13:16.170
I'd rather do it
when we can both be excited together.

13:25.012 --> 13:27.765
Neither of us have been
in a relationship this serious.

13:27.848 --> 13:29.058
Marriage and all.

13:29.141 --> 13:33.103
There's so many dumb things
that I've done, and you had to deal with.

13:33.187 --> 13:35.189
And I realized it, and I'm ashamed.

13:35.773 --> 13:38.651
I thought if I tried to be tough
and keep it in, then…

13:39.235 --> 13:40.569
it would be better for you.

13:42.112 --> 13:44.824
And I now know that I just made things
harder for you.

13:47.827 --> 13:48.828
Anyway…

13:50.287 --> 13:52.331
I'm gonna work very hard
to get better, Yu-jin.

13:58.963 --> 14:00.339
I want this to work.

14:01.215 --> 14:02.383
Hm?

14:02.967 --> 14:04.593
Oppa.

14:11.392 --> 14:13.394
You shouldn't go all morning
with an empty stomach.

14:13.477 --> 14:15.062
Could I get you some milk?

14:15.896 --> 14:16.981
Mm-hm.

14:17.064 --> 14:19.316
Good. Okay, get dressed now.

16:06.215 --> 16:08.217
Twelfth floor.

16:08.300 --> 16:09.677
- Doors opening.
- Oh.

16:12.805 --> 16:13.973
It's you.

16:14.056 --> 16:16.058
Ha-kyung.

16:20.437 --> 16:22.481
Uh, I'm, um… I'm here to, uh, go…

16:23.232 --> 16:25.025
- Because I--
- Eomma sent you?

16:25.109 --> 16:25.943
Huh?

16:30.155 --> 16:31.740
Doors closing.

16:32.825 --> 16:34.243
Doors opening.

16:34.827 --> 16:37.037
Come on, you're being too harsh.

16:37.121 --> 16:39.707
Our eomma only does this 'cause she cares.

16:39.790 --> 16:41.000
How can you defend her?

16:41.083 --> 16:43.460
There's no excuse
for her sending you this early!

16:43.544 --> 16:46.714
Sorry, I thought if I came early,
we'd have time to talk.

16:46.797 --> 16:48.841
We didn't realize you left so early.

16:48.924 --> 16:50.592
Why is she so obsessed?

16:50.676 --> 16:52.761
Why does it matter
if I get married or not?

16:53.262 --> 16:55.639
I said we broke up,
why doesn't she believe me?

16:55.723 --> 16:57.433
You what? Who's the guy?

16:58.600 --> 16:59.601
Go home.

17:00.102 --> 17:02.187
Eomma needs to stay away.
Can you tell her that for me?

17:02.271 --> 17:03.522
Actually, I'll call her.

17:03.605 --> 17:05.649
No, don't! You can't.

17:05.733 --> 17:07.234
Ma would kill me.

17:07.317 --> 17:09.903
What are you talking about?
And what did you do to her?

17:09.987 --> 17:10.863
Huh?

17:12.072 --> 17:15.409
Hey, I know how you are when you're mad.
You're gonna blow up at her.

17:15.492 --> 17:18.620
You say all this awful stuff,
and then run away.

17:18.704 --> 17:21.165
And she goes on for days.
I can't run away.

17:21.248 --> 17:23.667
She mopes around,
and comes up with a million plans.

17:23.751 --> 17:25.669
"This is the one!" Ugh!

17:25.753 --> 17:27.337
No, Jin Ha-kyung.

17:27.421 --> 17:30.716
I'm begging, take an hour to cool off
before you call her.

17:30.799 --> 17:33.886
It seems like a really bad idea
to make this call right now.

17:33.969 --> 17:35.012
I can't allow it.

17:35.095 --> 17:36.805
For my sake, you can't call her.

17:40.267 --> 17:41.560
Fine. All right.

17:43.896 --> 17:45.355
Sometimes you're great.

17:50.027 --> 17:51.695
I owe you one, or something.

17:53.113 --> 17:55.324
You didn't see me today. Get to work.

17:56.992 --> 17:58.410
I'll go first. Okay. See ya.

18:09.797 --> 18:10.839
Sweetheart.

18:12.174 --> 18:13.634
Take a look at this.

18:15.844 --> 18:16.929
What is it?

18:19.139 --> 18:20.849
Well, it's…

18:23.644 --> 18:25.020
Dear Bo-mi.

18:25.104 --> 18:26.105
Happy birthday!

18:26.188 --> 18:28.398
It's funny.

18:30.025 --> 18:32.361
Right? It doubles as an alarm, too.

18:32.444 --> 18:35.906
It can attach to her backpack.
You think she'll like it? Do you?

18:37.533 --> 18:38.951
Bo-mi is in seventh grade.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.744
I know. Are you messing with me?

18:40.828 --> 18:43.455
No, for her age,
the bear is not a great present.

18:46.041 --> 18:48.043
Really? They said it's the new thing.

18:48.127 --> 18:49.461
Ugh!

18:50.045 --> 18:51.672
I'm going to school.

18:51.755 --> 18:53.173
Not before you eat.

18:53.841 --> 18:55.467
My stomach's upset.

18:56.260 --> 18:57.344
Her stomach's upset?

18:57.427 --> 18:58.637
It's monthly.

18:59.721 --> 19:00.639
What?

19:00.722 --> 19:02.474
Bo-mi, at least drink this.

19:03.392 --> 19:04.434
It's monthly.

19:08.856 --> 19:10.524
Oh, it's her…

19:16.113 --> 19:18.365
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

19:18.448 --> 19:20.284
Hey, did you hear
that they're dating?

19:20.367 --> 19:22.035
- Really?
- Yeah.

19:22.119 --> 19:23.787
Really? They're dating?

19:25.789 --> 19:27.708
I heard it's Director Jin from Team Two.

19:28.458 --> 19:30.878
I HEARD THEY'RE DATING

19:30.961 --> 19:32.296
ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:33.297 --> 19:34.798
HOW LONG HAS IT BEEN?

19:34.882 --> 19:36.341
REALLY?
I HEARD HE'S WITH DIRECTOR JIN

19:36.425 --> 19:38.760
THEY LOOK GOOD TOGETHER

19:40.012 --> 19:43.098
THEY'RE GOING OUT

19:43.182 --> 19:44.600
THEY ARE?
THEY'RE REALLY DATING?

19:44.683 --> 19:46.393
REALLY? ANOTHER COLLEAGUE?

19:48.812 --> 19:50.856
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

20:04.244 --> 20:05.621
I heard they're dating.

20:05.704 --> 20:06.955
How long?

20:07.039 --> 20:08.290
Look.

20:10.500 --> 20:11.835
Do you know if it's true?

20:12.836 --> 20:15.547
Forecaster Lee Si-woo
and Director Jin Ha-kyung?

20:15.631 --> 20:17.090
They're really dating?

20:19.134 --> 20:20.802
You think
she'll get married this time?

20:20.886 --> 20:23.180
- They're great together.
- They're both good-looking.

20:48.080 --> 20:50.082
I really hope you thought this through.

20:50.791 --> 20:52.209
I guess you might as well.

20:52.876 --> 20:53.835
What?

20:55.295 --> 20:57.464
Director Ha-kyung isn't just a co-worker.

20:58.382 --> 21:01.426
We all saw what happened
her first time dating a co-worker.

21:01.510 --> 21:02.886
It was awful for her.

21:03.971 --> 21:06.348
You wouldn't call things off
just 'cause of the speculation,

21:06.431 --> 21:07.516
you like her a lot.

21:07.599 --> 21:10.394
They say, "Heavy is the head
that wears the crown." Right?

21:11.228 --> 21:13.772
- That's how it goes.
- I guess so.

21:15.649 --> 21:18.151
But, uh, Mrs. Oh, actually, we--

21:18.235 --> 21:21.238
You'll be fine. I'm rooting for you two.

21:22.614 --> 21:24.825
I hope everything works out.

21:25.534 --> 21:28.328
And of course, that Director Jin
won't get hurt again.

21:28.412 --> 21:30.330
It's good that she's
with someone like you.

21:31.415 --> 21:34.167
If she was headed for a Ki-jun repeat,
there's a chance that

21:34.251 --> 21:38.255
she could actually end up in Geneva,
so she can really start over.

21:39.339 --> 21:41.883
Oh, and between the two of us, uh, we…

21:41.967 --> 21:45.512
Well, Team Two cannot handle
another new director.

21:46.221 --> 21:47.431
Not this year.

21:48.390 --> 21:51.310
We're finally sort of beginning
to work well.

21:52.060 --> 21:53.061
Yeah.

21:54.187 --> 21:57.190
I'm sure that you both knew
going into things

21:57.274 --> 21:58.734
that it was worth all the risk.

21:59.693 --> 22:03.864
If it was just a fling or anything,
that wasn't serious, then, well…

22:04.489 --> 22:06.950
we never would've known.

22:07.034 --> 22:08.660
- Yeah.
- Mm.

22:10.120 --> 22:12.205
Don't let all the talk get to you.

22:13.749 --> 22:14.791
Okay?

22:14.875 --> 22:17.294
- Good luck, Si-woo.
- Okay. Thank you.

22:46.156 --> 22:47.407
What do you need?

22:49.451 --> 22:50.535
What do we do?

22:50.619 --> 22:54.289
Everyone thinks that we're really serious
about each other.

22:54.373 --> 22:55.540
Ignore it.

22:55.624 --> 22:58.043
Don't listen and don't comment.
Just ignore it.

22:58.126 --> 22:59.378
And then they'll move on.

22:59.461 --> 23:01.254
There will be a lot
of new gossips soon enough.

23:02.422 --> 23:05.217
- Yeah, or we could--
- If this isn't about work, I'm hanging up.

23:05.300 --> 23:07.928
You can't call me at work
to talk about this stuff.

23:32.994 --> 23:34.996
- Good work.
- Thank you, sir.

23:44.923 --> 23:46.633
- Great work, sir.
- Mm.

23:47.384 --> 23:48.844
What should we look out for?

23:49.636 --> 23:51.138
Yeah, well, there's not much today.

23:53.890 --> 23:56.435
The upper-level trough
around the Baikal

23:56.518 --> 23:58.979
seems to be developing unusually quickly.

23:59.062 --> 24:01.148
It will still be within a week or so.

24:01.231 --> 24:03.066
Some days
the weather's just great.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.486
And we got through the busy season,
which helps.

24:06.570 --> 24:08.697
You should go on a date with this weather.

24:11.700 --> 24:13.827
Well, there are many other things to do
in good weather.

24:14.411 --> 24:16.955
If things are slow
with live monitoring for today,

24:17.038 --> 24:20.417
you could look into the first frost dates
for the last 30 years.

24:20.500 --> 24:22.294
Get a head start for winter?

24:22.377 --> 24:24.588
You want to start right now?

24:25.464 --> 24:26.548
Oh, come on.

24:26.631 --> 24:29.092
We just cleared busy season.
Can't we breathe a little?

24:29.176 --> 24:32.053
Just 'cause it's over,
doesn't mean we can get complacent.

24:33.555 --> 24:36.183
There's always a cyclone
after a migratory anticyclone.

24:36.266 --> 24:38.018
The smallest change in the air current

24:38.101 --> 24:40.520
can lead to disaster,
so we've got to stay on our toes.

24:40.604 --> 24:43.732
Also, please keep things professional
when we're working.

24:45.233 --> 24:46.902
Of course, I will. I will.

24:47.486 --> 24:49.154
It was just a joke, though.

24:50.155 --> 24:52.199
You don't need to make
a big deal out of it.

25:36.993 --> 25:38.161
Oh, boy.

25:44.417 --> 25:46.253
You just got here or are you leaving?

25:46.336 --> 25:47.504
Uh…

25:48.338 --> 25:49.714
You remember Mi-seon, don't you?

25:49.798 --> 25:51.132
We went to middle school together.

25:51.216 --> 25:53.552
Yesterday, there was a party
for her newest book,

25:53.635 --> 25:56.054
and I had a drink or a few.

25:56.137 --> 25:57.597
She wrote another one?

25:57.681 --> 25:58.974
Oh.

25:59.057 --> 26:00.850
What are you gonna do?

26:01.434 --> 26:05.146
She's younger, published more.
Meanwhile, you've done what?

26:05.230 --> 26:07.315
So when are you gonna get a party?

26:08.066 --> 26:09.359
Well, really soon.

26:09.442 --> 26:11.486
I'm just working everything out right now.

26:11.570 --> 26:15.115
You don't ever know
if it'll happen till it's done.

26:15.198 --> 26:18.076
When are you going to get a real job?
This is too unreliable.

26:18.159 --> 26:20.287
One more year? How long?

26:20.370 --> 26:21.371
Eomma.

26:21.454 --> 26:23.331
I can write a bestseller. You don't know.

26:23.415 --> 26:26.167
Get the book finished
and show me the numbers.

26:26.251 --> 26:27.711
And then we can talk.

26:27.794 --> 26:28.670
Okay?

26:29.379 --> 26:32.048
Good grief.
I've got two perfectly capable kids.

26:32.132 --> 26:35.260
Why won't they let me help them
to be happy?

26:35.343 --> 26:38.138
Eomma, just leave Ha-kyung alone,
would you?

26:38.221 --> 26:41.516
Who cares who she's dating
or if she ever gets married?

26:41.600 --> 26:43.310
She lied to you about it, too?

26:43.393 --> 26:44.394
What?

26:44.477 --> 26:46.813
Ha-kyung's dating
the Team Two guy. I know.

26:46.896 --> 26:48.106
Team who?

26:48.189 --> 26:50.817
She's dating a co-worker? Who is it?

26:51.443 --> 26:52.652
It's that guy, you know.

26:52.736 --> 26:55.655
The tall one. He could be on TV.

26:55.739 --> 26:57.574
Pale face, he could be an actor.

26:58.283 --> 27:01.870
The only guy I know who…
Is it Shin Seok-ho?

27:01.953 --> 27:03.455
Shin Seok-ho now?

27:03.538 --> 27:05.749
The guy above Ha-kyung.
They're on the same…

27:05.832 --> 27:08.126
They both work on Team Two.

27:08.918 --> 27:10.962
That guy is not tall at all.

27:11.046 --> 27:13.089
He's pale, but he's not that handsome.

27:13.173 --> 27:15.842
I think he could definitely be an actor.

27:17.719 --> 27:21.181
Well, anyway, Eomma, who…
Who is she going with?

27:21.264 --> 27:22.849
Lee Si-woo is the guy.

27:24.059 --> 27:27.687
You know him. It's the guy
she had to go to Jeju with.

27:28.271 --> 27:31.024
I know for a fact
they've been seeing each other.

27:31.107 --> 27:33.735
And they think they can lie
to my face about it?

27:33.818 --> 27:35.236
Why wouldn't they lie?

27:35.320 --> 27:37.322
Eomma, you know how you are
with these things.

27:37.405 --> 27:38.615
What'd I do?

27:38.698 --> 27:41.326
"What's his family like?
What does his father do?"

27:41.409 --> 27:44.120
"What college? What's his level at work?"

27:44.204 --> 27:46.581
"What day was he born? What hour?"

27:46.665 --> 27:50.001
Ha-kyung told you that?
That I asked her about that stuff.

27:50.085 --> 27:52.712
No, Ha-kyung doesn't have to say a thing.

27:52.796 --> 27:54.798
You asked that about every guy
we've mentioned.

27:54.881 --> 27:56.966
It wasn't all of them.

27:57.467 --> 28:00.845
Eomma, you have to let it go.

28:00.929 --> 28:02.597
You only mess things up

28:02.681 --> 28:04.808
when you insert yourself
and manage her life.

28:05.767 --> 28:08.311
It's a big deal that she's dating at all.

28:08.395 --> 28:10.480
You should be excited just for that, huh?

28:10.563 --> 28:14.109
- I get it. Enough. I'll stop.
- Uh-huh?

28:14.192 --> 28:15.360
I just care!

28:17.946 --> 28:19.698
- Hang on.
- Hm?

28:19.781 --> 28:21.116
Where did you sleep last night?

28:21.199 --> 28:22.575
Oh, Shin Se…

28:24.703 --> 28:25.745
Shin's guest bed.

28:25.829 --> 28:27.205
Wasn't it Mi-seon's party?

28:27.789 --> 28:31.000
Uh, Shin came to the party, too.
There were lots of people there.

28:32.335 --> 28:34.170
You don't need to know any of that!

28:48.226 --> 28:50.520
It's terrifying that she can always tell.

28:53.565 --> 28:55.316
Hmm?

28:59.070 --> 29:00.780
Why did you sneak out
this morning?

29:00.864 --> 29:02.407
I was going to make you coffee.

29:11.291 --> 29:13.793
What are your plans
this evening?

29:20.675 --> 29:22.051
I'm totally free.

29:23.553 --> 29:25.305
- Mr. Um.
- Yeah?

29:25.388 --> 29:28.057
I've got the regional temperature analysis
you wanted.

29:28.141 --> 29:29.768
- I'll take a look.
- Okay.

29:29.851 --> 29:32.020
Oh, also, how old are your boys right now?

29:32.103 --> 29:34.564
The eldest is ten,
and the youngest is now eight.

29:34.647 --> 29:37.442
- Why?
- You probably wouldn't know, then.

29:37.525 --> 29:38.943
Huh? Know what?

29:39.652 --> 29:43.990
- Oh, I… Well, it's Bo-mi's birthday soon.
- Oh.

29:44.073 --> 29:47.744
And I have no idea
what kids that age are into.

29:47.827 --> 29:50.997
Ah, Bo-mi's in middle school.
So, what grade is she in?

29:51.080 --> 29:51.915
Seventh.

29:52.582 --> 29:53.792
Seventh.

29:53.875 --> 29:54.918
Brand-name things.

29:55.668 --> 29:57.295
Brand names?

29:57.378 --> 29:59.172
What are you talking about? She's a kid.

29:59.255 --> 30:01.007
Hm? Haven't you heard?

30:01.090 --> 30:04.427
Your teenagers all love brand names,
you know? It's the new thing.

30:05.011 --> 30:07.430
My niece said she wanted a Valen coat

30:07.514 --> 30:10.350
from her mom if she scored well
in the next PSAT coming up.

30:10.433 --> 30:11.643
For real?

30:13.853 --> 30:15.772
Tell me, aren't those real expensive?

30:15.855 --> 30:17.440
It's designer. Of course, it is.

30:17.524 --> 30:19.025
- Yeah, right?
- Mm.

30:20.985 --> 30:22.320
What the…

30:24.155 --> 30:25.907
They get this stuff for kids?

30:25.990 --> 30:28.701
Wow, this is crazy expensive.

30:28.785 --> 30:31.246
I haven't even looked at a coat
that costs so much money.

30:31.329 --> 30:33.790
Just for a coat?

30:33.873 --> 30:34.999
Soo-jin.

30:35.083 --> 30:37.752
Could you look at the data
for the migratory cyclone movement

30:37.836 --> 30:40.129
for September to October
from the last decade?

30:40.213 --> 30:42.632
Huh? The whole decade?

30:43.216 --> 30:44.425
Yes. The whole thing, please.

30:47.136 --> 30:48.096
Okay.

30:50.932 --> 30:52.892
Wow, what do I…

30:52.976 --> 30:54.769
You don't have to spend
that kind of money.

30:55.270 --> 30:56.980
There are plenty
of other things she'll love.

30:57.564 --> 30:59.357
How does anyone afford a coat like that?

31:00.191 --> 31:02.944
- Jeez.
- Do they wear it to school?

31:04.404 --> 31:05.947
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

31:08.700 --> 31:10.410
Well, have you thought about it?

31:13.705 --> 31:15.707
Ms. Im took a leave of absence?

31:15.790 --> 31:17.458
- Mm-hm.
- Why?

31:17.542 --> 31:19.460
Her husband was transferred
to the US branch,

31:19.544 --> 31:22.005
- so she's moving out there for a bit.
- Mm…

31:22.088 --> 31:24.173
So, we'll need someone to fill in.

31:24.757 --> 31:25.633
Right.

31:26.926 --> 31:30.555
I was thinking, you said you wanted
to transfer over to Policy, right?

31:30.638 --> 31:33.433
I do. You don't know
how many times I've applied.

31:34.017 --> 31:36.019
I think you should give it another shot.

31:36.102 --> 31:39.022
The director, right now,
I think he'd take you in a second.

31:39.105 --> 31:40.982
- Seriously?
- Mm-hmm.

31:46.279 --> 31:48.615
SOO-JIN, HAVE YOU MADE UP YOUR MIND?

31:55.580 --> 31:58.708
Who's currently working
on the 24-hour forecast?

32:00.793 --> 32:01.878
I am.

32:07.675 --> 32:09.260
How long till we can send it out?

32:09.344 --> 32:12.347
Hmm, it'll be done in an hour, I'd say.

32:15.892 --> 32:18.937
I also need that cyclone development data
from Baikal Lake.

32:19.520 --> 32:21.105
I'll have them for you soon as well.

32:22.774 --> 32:26.027
I'm putting it on a chart.
That way, it'll be easier to look at.

32:30.782 --> 32:32.283
No, that's okay. Just the data.

32:32.867 --> 32:35.453
- It's not hard to do.
- Just the data.

32:35.536 --> 32:36.663
Okay.

32:44.253 --> 32:46.172
Ignore him. Focus.

32:53.054 --> 32:56.015
Mr. Kim, would you go
to the Model Department right now

32:56.099 --> 32:58.142
and get me the data
on the three-month outlook?

33:02.146 --> 33:03.022
Mr. Kim.

33:03.606 --> 33:06.275
That kid is so distracted.
He never pays attention.

33:11.990 --> 33:16.035
When did Director Jin Ha-kyung
and Forecaster Lee Si-woo start dating?

33:16.119 --> 33:18.329
You know what they say,
misery loves company.

33:18.413 --> 33:21.499
That reporter Chae Yu-jin used to date
Lee Si-woo before she got married.

33:21.582 --> 33:23.292
Wait. So that's not a love triangle.

33:23.376 --> 33:25.628
- A love square?
- It's something, for sure.

33:25.712 --> 33:26.587
Too much free time?

33:27.255 --> 33:29.340
Sir.

33:30.842 --> 33:32.427
Oh, I'm sorry, sir.

33:33.177 --> 33:35.471
I don't say anything. Ever.

33:39.809 --> 33:41.227
Go to the Model Department,

33:41.310 --> 33:42.979
see what they have
for the next three months

33:43.062 --> 33:44.522
and bring it back here, please.

33:44.605 --> 33:45.523
Yep.

33:56.409 --> 33:59.203
Do you think Mr. Han
and Ms. Chae know?

33:59.287 --> 34:00.955
Everyone's heard by now.

34:01.039 --> 34:03.708
That's why you shouldn't date co-workers.

34:56.385 --> 34:58.638
The climate outlook report
for this winter…

34:59.388 --> 35:02.308
I think you'll need to add more
on the possibility of a La Niña.

35:02.391 --> 35:03.601
LA NIÑA: A PHENOMENON IN THE EQUATORIAL
REGION OF THE EASTERN PACIFIC OCEAN"

35:03.684 --> 35:06.020
Okay. Is it because of the NOAA?

35:06.104 --> 35:07.480
It's not just them.

35:08.231 --> 35:10.900
The ECWMF, the Australian,
and the Japanese forecasts

35:10.983 --> 35:12.902
have La Niña predictions this winter.

35:13.653 --> 35:15.947
Whatever we're saying,
I need it by four o'clock.

35:16.447 --> 35:18.407
If you can get it in any earlier,
that'd be great.

35:32.880 --> 35:34.048
Is there something else?

35:37.093 --> 35:39.220
It looks like
there's something you want to say.

35:45.476 --> 35:49.856
I've known Ha-kyung for over ten years,
that's a while.

35:49.939 --> 35:52.358
In that time, I got too used to her.

35:53.025 --> 35:55.444
It was too easy to forget
how amazing she is.

35:55.528 --> 35:57.155
I came to take her for granted.

35:58.531 --> 36:00.741
I completely lost perspective on her.

36:00.825 --> 36:04.328
When I should've realized what we had
and been thankful,

36:04.412 --> 36:06.622
I got further from reality
and more resentful.

36:07.373 --> 36:09.125
What are you telling me exactly?

36:12.837 --> 36:15.548
I was really the asshole
in our story together.

36:18.134 --> 36:20.219
And it's different from the two of you.

36:20.303 --> 36:22.638
Ha-kyung will have trouble
moving on from you.

36:28.728 --> 36:30.479
Well, uh, she broke it off.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.440
You think that will get you off the hook?

36:34.692 --> 36:38.196
Nobody really cares if you're together
or if you're not, you know that?

36:39.322 --> 36:43.201
What they wanna know
is the reason why it happened.

36:46.454 --> 36:50.458
When you date in the office,
or have any kind of drama,

36:51.125 --> 36:55.838
somehow, women always end up
getting hit harder than the men do.

36:55.922 --> 37:00.593
So Ha-kyung didn't just get hurt by me,
the office was judging her as well.

37:00.676 --> 37:01.886
But…

37:03.012 --> 37:05.264
you've had a taste of how that is, too.

37:05.973 --> 37:09.560
She really shouldn't have to deal
with all that gossip any longer.

37:10.144 --> 37:12.521
- I know that.
- So then…

37:15.566 --> 37:18.069
I'm the last person
who should be saying this.

37:19.445 --> 37:21.906
Fight the break up
unless you're totally sure.

37:24.242 --> 37:28.037
If you're sure that things are ending,
do what you can to help her.

37:30.248 --> 37:32.208
Do the opposite of what I did.

37:43.761 --> 37:46.472
The cold weather could hit
the south sooner than we thought.

37:46.555 --> 37:48.724
We'll ask
the Forecast Analysis team first.

37:48.808 --> 37:51.894
And then, if it's confirmed,
we'll tell Impact Forecast right away.

37:52.436 --> 37:53.396
All right.

37:54.981 --> 37:57.692
What are you saying?
That it's gonna be cold?

37:58.234 --> 38:01.737
In Siberia, the anticyclone
is developing faster than expected,

38:01.821 --> 38:03.698
so the temperature will drop.

38:03.781 --> 38:06.826
Look here, the core of the cold wave,
it's headed in that direction.

38:06.909 --> 38:10.288
So the North Atlantic anticyclone
has migrated away to the east,

38:10.371 --> 38:13.708
and that cold continental anticyclone
from the lake is speeding up.

38:14.583 --> 38:16.377
In those positions, it will get cold.

38:16.460 --> 38:17.795
What about near Daegwallyeong?

38:17.878 --> 38:21.340
It looks like the temperature
will go below zero inland by tomorrow,

38:21.424 --> 38:23.509
around Daegwallyeong and Cheorwon.

38:23.592 --> 38:25.886
Mr. Shin, what was our forecast
for this week?

38:26.387 --> 38:29.140
We've predicted that the temperatures
in those particular areas

38:29.223 --> 38:30.725
will drop this weekend.

38:30.808 --> 38:33.394
If the temperature drops
by 10 degrees or more,

38:33.477 --> 38:35.354
the sudden change
will feel like a big shock.

38:35.438 --> 38:37.440
He's right. That's not good.

38:40.151 --> 38:42.528
It'll impact the farmers
all over the country.

38:42.611 --> 38:43.696
They're about to harvest.

38:44.405 --> 38:47.325
It's almost kimchi season.
So the radishes on Ganghwa Island

38:47.408 --> 38:50.119
and the cabbage crop in Gangwon
could be severely damaged,

38:50.703 --> 38:54.081
plus the soybeans and chili peppers
from North Gyeongsang, too.

38:55.624 --> 38:58.586
We'll monitor for a little longer
and see if there's a clear pattern,

38:58.669 --> 39:00.629
and decide if we need a warning
and when to send it out.

39:00.713 --> 39:03.132
For the farmers, reach out
to the local governments,

39:03.215 --> 39:04.550
warn them to prepare for the cold.

39:04.633 --> 39:06.010
They'll do what they can.

39:06.093 --> 39:09.263
But if a cyclone was developing this fast
with those temperatures,

39:09.972 --> 39:12.641
I would've expected your team
to notify us sooner.

39:13.434 --> 39:16.979
I guess we all know how it is
with a new boyfriend, right?

39:20.733 --> 39:22.651
- Hey, Mr. Kim.
- Huh?

39:22.735 --> 39:24.153
How's your wife these days?

39:24.737 --> 39:26.280
- Good.
- Great.

39:27.740 --> 39:30.785
Did you know Mrs. Kim
used to work at the KMA?

39:32.036 --> 39:33.454
Hm, so she did.

39:33.537 --> 39:37.458
I remember you two
had a… whirlwind romance, didn't you?

39:37.541 --> 39:40.378
Oh, remember all the PDA?
And whenever you fought,

39:40.461 --> 39:42.546
the whole office held their breath?

39:42.630 --> 39:44.840
Yeah, everyone
was so scared of you two.

39:44.924 --> 39:47.259
- 'Cause if they broke up… Ugh!
- What a huge deal.

39:47.343 --> 39:49.929
Well, anyway, I should head
to the Spokesperson's Office.

39:50.012 --> 39:51.889
We'll reach out
to those local governments.

39:53.891 --> 39:57.561
He's having a day. It's a mid-life crisis.

39:57.645 --> 39:58.938
I'll talk to him, okay?

40:02.066 --> 40:04.318
You didn't have to do that, Mr. Um.

40:04.402 --> 40:08.114
I did. Otherwise, people
would just keep disrespecting you.

40:10.074 --> 40:11.200
He's right.

40:11.283 --> 40:13.494
We're here to work, not to make jokes.

40:13.577 --> 40:16.372
He should know better
than to comment on your personal life.

40:16.455 --> 40:18.082
Please, he does know better.

40:19.041 --> 40:21.919
So, there's a cold wave coming in, right?

40:22.545 --> 40:23.838
Let's get to work.

40:23.921 --> 40:25.673
I have something to say first.

40:28.634 --> 40:29.552
We have…

40:34.306 --> 40:36.183
Forecaster Lee Si-woo and I--

40:36.267 --> 40:38.477
Thank you for all your support.

40:39.854 --> 40:42.731
We're just here to work. Keep it separate.

40:44.150 --> 40:45.359
Was that it?

40:48.404 --> 40:49.447
Yeah.

40:49.530 --> 40:51.115
Okay.

40:52.408 --> 40:54.201
No PDA, okay, you two?

40:56.495 --> 40:58.205
Ooh!

41:15.973 --> 41:18.601
Why did you say that in there?
What was that?

41:19.185 --> 41:21.937
Let's keep it… a secret for a while.

41:22.021 --> 41:23.022
What?

41:23.105 --> 41:24.315
That we're not together.

41:24.398 --> 41:25.649
What are you saying?

41:27.234 --> 41:29.236
You know, it'll be so annoying,

41:29.320 --> 41:33.574
if people think we just started dating,
and then we break up right away.

41:33.657 --> 41:36.952
Everyone is going to speculate
about what went wrong so quickly.

41:37.036 --> 41:39.079
It's just asking for extra gossip.

41:39.663 --> 41:43.125
So I thought we should pretend
we're still dating for a while.

41:43.709 --> 41:45.002
So it won't be such a big deal.

41:45.753 --> 41:46.837
You're trying to spare me?

41:49.882 --> 41:52.760
You're trying to protect me
from everyone from the gossip?

41:52.843 --> 41:53.761
That's the idea?

41:55.304 --> 41:56.305
It's not…

41:57.723 --> 42:00.643
Then it's because right now
you look like the villain?

42:00.726 --> 42:02.811
- It's not.
- There has to be something.

42:02.895 --> 42:04.396
I just don't want to hear it.

42:05.439 --> 42:08.567
I don't wanna hear people talking
about you like they really know.

42:08.651 --> 42:10.611
'Cause I can't handle anymore.

42:12.905 --> 42:14.031
That's why.

42:16.909 --> 42:19.828
You didn't know? That's what happens
when you date in the office.

42:20.496 --> 42:22.873
Whether it ends in marriage
or incredible heartbreak,

42:22.957 --> 42:25.501
they all turn it into gossip
for the group chat.

42:27.711 --> 42:29.380
I knew that going in.

42:31.173 --> 42:33.634
Still, I chose to do it again.

42:41.225 --> 42:42.810
- I'm sorry.
- Don't say that to me.

42:43.435 --> 42:44.979
I knew the risks.

42:45.062 --> 42:48.023
I chose to start it. It's my own doing.

42:49.608 --> 42:51.151
So don't say you're sorry.

42:51.235 --> 42:55.114
What happens from here
isn't anything I haven't seen before.

42:55.698 --> 42:57.366
It's not for you, though.

43:00.786 --> 43:03.497
I struggle with everything.

43:06.208 --> 43:07.376
It's been awful.

43:09.878 --> 43:11.755
I didn't want you to get hurt,

43:12.506 --> 43:14.341
just because I can't play clingy.

43:15.050 --> 43:15.926
I didn't know…

43:17.928 --> 43:21.307
doing that would hurt you even more.

43:49.335 --> 43:50.461
Chae Yu-jin.

43:52.296 --> 43:54.256
The column is yours from now on.

43:55.049 --> 43:56.050
Hm?

43:57.009 --> 43:59.470
Isn't this the special article Se-hui
was working on?

44:00.429 --> 44:04.141
She's with child.
She needs to take it easy for a while.

44:04.725 --> 44:06.769
Wow. She's having a baby?

44:09.313 --> 44:11.732
She thinks she's so special for it.

44:11.815 --> 44:14.193
And she didn't apologize for anything.

44:15.486 --> 44:17.404
Well, she's probably nervous about it all.

44:18.280 --> 44:20.949
I wish she'd take a leave of absence
till she has the thing.

44:21.533 --> 44:24.244
At least we could get a temporary
or something if she did that.

44:24.328 --> 44:26.664
It's inconsiderate,
and we're stuck with her.

44:27.498 --> 44:29.708
How long am I in charge of the column?

44:29.792 --> 44:31.251
It's yours now.

44:32.336 --> 44:33.253
What?

44:33.921 --> 44:36.590
It's on you. You've got it forever.

44:37.383 --> 44:42.137
Realistically, having a kid means
that she won't get back to work

44:42.221 --> 44:43.347
for a year or two.

44:43.847 --> 44:46.308
Women do that,
and they get out of practice.

44:46.392 --> 44:47.976
Article quality goes down.

44:48.060 --> 44:50.979
And if they can't catch up,
they get kicked to the curve, you know?

44:51.063 --> 44:53.190
There's no way.

44:53.691 --> 44:56.068
I only mean that she'll get back, and…

44:58.195 --> 45:00.030
What? You don't believe it?

45:00.948 --> 45:02.366
Ask anyone here.

45:02.449 --> 45:07.204
Do you know how many reporters
never come back after kids?

45:08.163 --> 45:11.875
This is a great opportunity for you,
so don't mess it up.

45:13.127 --> 45:15.379
You always said you wanted
your own column.

45:16.004 --> 45:19.341
This column is on the front page, my dear.

45:19.883 --> 45:21.135
That's a great spot.

45:23.470 --> 45:24.513
Yeah.

45:25.347 --> 45:26.390
Thank you, sir.

45:27.933 --> 45:29.727
Okay. Get to it.

45:46.994 --> 45:49.955
Penny for your thoughts?
You look so pretty.

45:50.038 --> 45:52.666
Nothing.

45:54.251 --> 45:56.670
Really? What's going on?

45:59.423 --> 46:02.342
They gave the column to me,
so there's that.

46:02.426 --> 46:03.469
Seriously?

46:03.552 --> 46:05.971
Are you kidding?
Yu-jin, really, it's all yours?

46:07.389 --> 46:09.767
Oh, why the face? That's fantastic.

46:10.309 --> 46:11.477
Oh…

46:11.560 --> 46:14.021
Oh, I have this briefing now,
and then I'm off.

46:14.563 --> 46:16.315
Let's go and grab a drink to celebrate.

46:16.982 --> 46:18.275
I can't have alcohol.

46:18.358 --> 46:21.153
Why? Still not feeling well?

46:24.156 --> 46:26.283
What is it, Yu-jin? Please tell me.

46:26.366 --> 46:27.451
I can handle it.

46:28.911 --> 46:30.621
What, you need a computer?

46:30.704 --> 46:32.873
Or a new purse? We can go to the mall.

46:34.666 --> 46:35.834
I'm…

46:36.418 --> 46:37.795
I'm pregnant.

46:45.344 --> 46:46.220
Huh?

46:47.221 --> 46:48.931
I'm 12 weeks along.

46:57.815 --> 47:01.401
Good job, everybody.
Let's call it a little early.

47:01.985 --> 47:04.154
- Okay.
- Okay.

47:43.110 --> 47:43.986
Hmm.

47:45.070 --> 47:46.697
Running late, Mr. Shin?

47:46.780 --> 47:48.407
Huh? Oh, uh…

47:49.449 --> 47:51.743
You're gaming, aren't you? Good luck.

47:51.827 --> 47:54.538
- No. Um…
- Where are you going, then?

47:55.247 --> 47:57.332
Is it a blind date? Is it?

47:58.709 --> 48:00.752
- It's not.
- What is it?

48:00.836 --> 48:02.796
- Doors opening.
- He said no?

48:07.301 --> 48:08.302
Hello.

48:12.222 --> 48:13.140
Huh.

48:14.600 --> 48:16.476
You're the last one.

48:17.561 --> 48:18.604
No.

48:19.271 --> 48:21.940
I have a very important appointment today.

48:22.024 --> 48:23.108
Hey.

48:25.485 --> 48:26.486
I'll get off.

48:28.864 --> 48:30.407
- Okay.
- Excuse me.

48:45.672 --> 48:46.882
This is so weird.

48:47.674 --> 48:49.051
I didn't notice.

48:50.719 --> 48:54.556
How long are we gonna act
like we're still together?

48:54.640 --> 48:56.266
Just until…

48:56.934 --> 48:58.727
they stop talking about it.

49:05.484 --> 49:07.152
You really want us to lie?

49:07.235 --> 49:08.278
Yes.

49:09.071 --> 49:10.072
I prefer it for now.

49:25.003 --> 49:26.880
HAN KI-JUN

49:35.097 --> 49:36.890
CHAE YU-JIN

49:50.320 --> 49:51.279
Welcome.

50:33.196 --> 50:34.948
Huh? Hey!

50:36.491 --> 50:37.701
Oh!

50:40.454 --> 50:41.747
I thought the traffic was…

50:41.830 --> 50:45.667
Yeah, the traffic was awful,
so you took the subway.

50:45.751 --> 50:47.794
You got off too early, yeah?

50:54.134 --> 50:55.886
So, do you wanna go eat?

51:07.647 --> 51:09.191
- Aah!
- Oh, god. God!

51:09.274 --> 51:11.568
Sorry, sorry, sorry. What did I do? Okay.

51:11.651 --> 51:14.237
- Ow! My hair.
- Oh, god. Wait, wait, wait. I'm sorry.

51:14.821 --> 51:17.365
- There. I got it. Are you okay?
- That hurt.

51:17.449 --> 51:19.201
I'm so sorry.

51:26.333 --> 51:27.501
Ow! Ow!

51:30.837 --> 51:31.880
Oh! What happened?

51:31.963 --> 51:34.341
It's okay. I'm so sorry.

51:34.966 --> 51:36.510
What do I do?

51:51.066 --> 51:53.819
You must think I'm an idiot.

51:54.319 --> 51:55.987
Mm-hmm. You're an idiot.

51:56.071 --> 51:57.906
I just didn't know what to do,

51:58.698 --> 52:01.368
the right thing to say,
or how I should be reacting.

52:03.662 --> 52:06.039
I barely managed to say anything at all.

52:12.796 --> 52:15.006
Still, I don't know how he…

52:15.507 --> 52:17.884
I tell him I'm pregnant
and he says that to me.

52:18.468 --> 52:19.636
Oh, uh…

52:20.387 --> 52:23.723
I-I thought…
that we are waiting to do… that.

52:23.807 --> 52:26.434
Why would he say that?

52:27.936 --> 52:29.396
What were you expecting?

52:30.397 --> 52:33.650
I mean, I don't know.
Something better than that.

52:34.151 --> 52:35.735
That he always wanted to be a dad.

52:35.819 --> 52:37.529
Or, "How are you feeling?"

52:37.612 --> 52:39.030
Something supportive.

52:45.745 --> 52:47.831
What? Okay.

52:50.083 --> 52:52.961
You love him a lot, don't you?

52:56.339 --> 52:57.841
I thought he'd be better since he's older.

52:57.924 --> 53:00.969
Instead, he's like a teenager,
ever since the wedding.

53:01.553 --> 53:02.804
He's so immature.

53:04.431 --> 53:07.100
I thought marriage would be easy
and he'd take care of me.

53:07.642 --> 53:08.894
But this is harder.

53:09.936 --> 53:11.897
It feels like he's getting
more and more distant.

53:13.148 --> 53:14.983
And we fight all the time.

53:18.320 --> 53:20.238
No relationship is easy.

53:20.822 --> 53:23.909
If we can't get along
with our own parents, then…

53:24.576 --> 53:26.661
It's never been easy with my dad.

53:28.496 --> 53:31.875
Parents, children,
married couples, siblings…

53:31.958 --> 53:33.877
Things only get tougher with time.

53:34.586 --> 53:35.754
And with family.

53:35.837 --> 53:37.714
You expect more from them,

53:38.965 --> 53:40.258
so you get upset.

53:43.803 --> 53:45.764
Feels like I made the right choice.

53:47.599 --> 53:49.184
I'll never go through this with a wife.

53:51.895 --> 53:52.812
Right?

53:53.897 --> 53:56.650
Why? Something happened with the Director?

54:00.487 --> 54:02.656
It's over. We're done.

54:07.994 --> 54:10.914
If she's 12 weeks along, there's plenty
of time before the baby comes

54:10.997 --> 54:12.582
to apologize and prepare.

54:13.166 --> 54:14.668
Yeah, what about the money?

54:15.460 --> 54:18.672
Even now, we're stretched thin
with rent and bills.

54:19.673 --> 54:22.008
All right, but don't think of telling her
you'll go halfsies.

54:22.092 --> 54:24.511
English preschools are so expensive.

54:25.804 --> 54:27.847
You're getting a few years
ahead of yourself.

54:27.931 --> 54:30.725
You have to start them
when they're young, or else…

54:30.809 --> 54:32.143
And I can't teach them.

54:37.691 --> 54:39.317
You are excited, though.

54:42.362 --> 54:44.572
I feel…

54:46.074 --> 54:48.785
worried more than excited. What if I…

54:50.245 --> 54:51.538
I'm a bad dad.

54:52.497 --> 54:55.750
I barely even know
how to not be an awful husband.

55:00.422 --> 55:01.715
You'll be a good dad.

55:05.552 --> 55:06.720
You're gonna be great.

55:08.346 --> 55:11.725
You always do the best you can
when you care about things.

55:12.309 --> 55:15.103
If only I wasn't such
a picky perfectionist.

55:20.025 --> 55:22.694
So things with Lee Si-woo
went south, I heard.

55:29.743 --> 55:31.077
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung.

55:34.706 --> 55:37.292
One person wanting a relationship
isn't enough.

55:37.792 --> 55:40.253
What do you say is the reason?
That doesn't make sense.

55:41.796 --> 55:45.050
Oh, you know, he gave lots of reasons.
This and that.

55:45.133 --> 55:46.718
But it was that…

55:47.427 --> 55:48.845
I wasn't good enough.

55:48.928 --> 55:52.682
What… There's no way.
You're the coolest person I know.

55:53.266 --> 55:54.267
Huh?

55:54.351 --> 55:58.229
You're intelligent, good at your job,
responsible, really good at sports.

55:58.313 --> 56:01.107
If you don't know you're a ten,
I don't know how to help you.

56:02.859 --> 56:05.070
- You dumped me, too.
- Huh?

56:09.783 --> 56:11.368
Oh, that's just…

56:11.451 --> 56:13.370
It's fine. That's all over now.

56:15.497 --> 56:17.749
It's strange that it ended
like that twice.

56:18.333 --> 56:20.543
It's a sign that I'm bad at relationships.

56:21.127 --> 56:22.170
Hey.

56:23.296 --> 56:24.798
So tell your wife you're sorry.

56:24.881 --> 56:26.424
And don't drink anymore.

56:26.508 --> 56:29.177
Go get her flowers
or some other nice things from the store.

56:29.260 --> 56:31.429
Go now. Good night.

56:32.764 --> 56:34.349
It's 'cause I'm an idiot.

56:35.558 --> 56:37.602
You couldn't have been more wonderful.

56:40.021 --> 56:42.565
You're a real catch,
you know, Jin Ha-kyung?

56:48.154 --> 56:49.197
Good night.

57:12.470 --> 57:14.055
LEE SI-WOO'S FATHER

57:20.311 --> 57:21.438
Hello?

57:22.313 --> 57:23.773
There wasn't a day

57:24.441 --> 57:27.277
I didn't wish my father was different.

57:27.944 --> 57:29.446
But there was nothing I can do.

57:30.196 --> 57:31.698
My eomma and appa…

57:34.159 --> 57:35.702
acted like I…

57:36.286 --> 57:38.288
I did something wrong by being born.

57:39.664 --> 57:41.082
It was all my fault.

57:43.751 --> 57:45.712
It was my fault that my mom

57:47.046 --> 57:49.174
had to give up her work and stay home.

57:50.049 --> 57:52.510
My fault she got sick and passed away.

57:53.636 --> 57:56.931
He said she would've lived a long life
if I never came along.

57:59.767 --> 58:00.977
She only died,

58:02.187 --> 58:04.147
because I took so much out of her.

58:04.898 --> 58:06.149
That's terrible.

58:07.942 --> 58:10.278
If you can't handle that,
don't have a kid.

58:11.362 --> 58:12.614
It's awful

58:13.615 --> 58:16.451
when the people that brought you
into this world think

58:19.078 --> 58:20.663
you're what's wrong.

58:39.599 --> 58:40.683
Oh, honey.

58:41.351 --> 58:42.227
Sorry.

58:44.771 --> 58:46.022
My mom's worse.

58:46.105 --> 58:48.650
More than we thought
she'd be at this point.

58:49.275 --> 58:51.903
Uh-huh. Se-chan and I are coming home.

58:53.613 --> 58:56.950
Oh, honey, the bus is here.
I'll call you back, okay?

59:03.456 --> 59:05.124
I'm sorry, just a second.

59:06.876 --> 59:08.253
Here, I can get that.

59:08.336 --> 59:10.672
Oh, thank you. Thank you so much.

59:15.093 --> 59:17.345
- Oh, get on.
- Okay. Thank you.

59:22.225 --> 59:25.395
Don't cry, Se-chan. Aw, it's okay.

59:30.567 --> 59:32.235
I'm sorry, she's tired.

59:35.363 --> 59:36.990
Aw, it's okay.

59:39.284 --> 59:44.247
Realistically, having a kid means
that she won't get back to work

59:44.330 --> 59:45.415
for a year or two.

59:45.999 --> 59:48.543
Women do that,
and they get out of practice.

59:48.626 --> 59:50.086
Article quality goes down.

59:50.169 --> 59:53.464
And if they can't catch up, they're
getting kicked to the curve, you know?

01:00:08.730 --> 01:00:09.981
Welcome home.

01:00:11.316 --> 01:00:13.276
You must be tired. I'll hide that up.

01:00:14.736 --> 01:00:15.778
Why?

01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:23.161
I haven't congratulated you yet.

01:00:23.661 --> 01:00:25.163
I'm sorry about before.

01:00:25.705 --> 01:00:27.665
I freaked out. I was an idiot.

01:00:28.750 --> 01:00:30.460
I was surprised, that's all.

01:00:34.964 --> 01:00:36.633
I'm sorry it's been so hard.

01:00:36.716 --> 01:00:38.301
Especially for you.

01:00:38.885 --> 01:00:40.428
I love you, Yu-jin.

01:00:50.647 --> 01:00:52.523
I have an appointment
with the doctor next week.

01:00:54.901 --> 01:00:55.902
Y-You do?

01:00:56.486 --> 01:00:57.779
When? What day?

01:00:57.862 --> 01:00:59.947
I should be there, too. I'll come with.

01:01:03.076 --> 01:01:05.411
I was thinking
we shouldn't see it through.

01:01:06.412 --> 01:01:08.581
I don't know
how we'd take care of the kid.

01:01:13.086 --> 01:01:14.587
What are you saying then?

01:01:15.630 --> 01:01:17.465
You know you don't want it either.

01:01:18.091 --> 01:01:21.344
You're so stressed about money. And this…

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:23.763
It's not a good idea.

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:27.642
Yu-jin, are we gonna…

01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:30.353
We're not ready, oppa.

01:01:30.436 --> 01:01:31.521
Hm?

01:02:10.143 --> 01:02:11.686
There's no such thing…

01:02:13.229 --> 01:02:14.939
as guaranteed happiness.

01:02:16.190 --> 01:02:17.692
That's why I had to leave.

01:02:18.192 --> 01:02:19.902
I've tried so hard and I…

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:23.364
I can't figure out
how to be happy in life.

01:02:25.283 --> 01:02:26.117
And I couldn't…

01:02:27.660 --> 01:02:30.037
live with sharing any unhappiness
with her.

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:32.749
That's why.

01:02:49.223 --> 01:02:51.017
Oh, uh, good evening, ma'am.

01:02:53.060 --> 01:02:55.396
This is so weird.
I happened to be in the neighborhood--

01:02:55.480 --> 01:02:56.981
Where's Ha-kyung right now?

01:02:57.064 --> 01:02:58.149
What?

01:02:58.232 --> 01:03:00.318
Where's Ha-kyung? Was she with you?

01:03:09.118 --> 01:03:11.287
I'm looking for Lee Myung-han.

01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:12.830
Of course, one moment.

01:03:12.914 --> 01:03:15.583
Are you Mr. Lee's guardian?

01:03:18.044 --> 01:03:18.961
Uh, sort of.

01:03:20.046 --> 01:03:21.798
We brought him in from a car accident.

01:03:22.298 --> 01:03:25.176
And when we ran some of the basic tests,

01:03:25.259 --> 01:03:26.886
we found something that looks off.

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:29.806
- Is it an issue?
- Uh, yeah.

01:03:34.811 --> 01:03:36.521
LEE SI-WOO

01:03:44.570 --> 01:03:47.323
Answer your phone. Please, please.

01:04:02.296 --> 01:04:03.214
Hey, you.

01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:06.092
Oh, yes?

01:04:06.175 --> 01:04:08.052
I've wanted to chat with you.

01:04:08.636 --> 01:04:10.263
Hm. Sure.

01:04:12.265 --> 01:04:14.976
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

01:04:15.059 --> 01:04:16.477
LEE SI-WOO

01:04:24.527 --> 01:04:27.363
The weather's been pleasant
the past few days.

01:04:27.446 --> 01:04:29.448
However, an unexpected cold snap

01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:31.784
coming in may cause
some trouble for farmers.

01:04:31.868 --> 01:04:33.995
Cold weather encourages us staying in,

01:04:34.078 --> 01:04:36.998
withdrawing not just physically,
but mentally as well.

01:04:37.081 --> 01:04:39.375
We recommend that everyone
at home take extra care

01:04:39.458 --> 01:04:41.794
to maintain their immune system
and their mental health.

01:05:31.052 --> 01:05:32.929
So then, when do we expect it to end?

01:05:33.012 --> 01:05:34.055
As things stand--

01:05:34.138 --> 01:05:36.390
The forecast will have
to be reversed possibly.

01:05:36.474 --> 01:05:38.517
You're going to take a bullet
for what Si-woo said?

01:05:38.601 --> 01:05:39.560
Say that again!

01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.479
- Oh, uh…
- Hey, knock it off!

01:05:42.480 --> 01:05:44.148
Did you already know?

01:05:44.231 --> 01:05:45.274
You need a biopsy.

01:05:45.358 --> 01:05:47.276
My relationships
always started out great

01:05:47.360 --> 01:05:50.071
but my father would always ruin them.

01:05:50.154 --> 01:05:51.656
Because you'll regret it.

01:05:51.739 --> 01:05:54.408
You might regret it later.

01:05:54.492 --> 01:05:56.202
I still like you a lot.

01:05:57.453 --> 01:05:58.412
Do you know that?
